  data:  # 407c
    kind: invariant  # 407c
    title: "llvm_ir.py credits an indirect call to the first @name anywhere in the instruction: call void %fp(ptr @g) yields an edge to the global @g"  # 407c
    status: violated  # 407c
    priority: 3  # 407c
    parent:  # 407c
    tags:  # 407c
    - analysis_quality  # 407c
    - call_resolution  # 407c
    isbefore: []  # 407c
    duplicate_of: []  # 407c
    not_duplicate_of: []  # 407c
    pr_ref:  # 407c
    description: "Found by the 2026-10-06 docstring audit tail pass; reviewer reproduced: 'call void %fp(ptr @g)' produces ind -> g:variable. An indirect call should yield no resolved edge (or an unresolved one), not an edge to an argument."  # 407c
    fields:  # 407c
      statement: "A call edge's dst is the callee, never an argument."  # 407c
      root_cause: "_get_call_target (~L97) takes the first @name token in the call instruction rather than the callee operand, so for an indirect call through %fp it picks an argument."  # 407c
